<title>SWEDEN: Sandvik posts 18 pct fall in 9 mo profit.</title>
<headline>Sandvik posts 18 pct fall in 9 mo profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish engineer and tool maker Sandvik results for the nine months ending September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		  3,540 vs   4,306</p>
<p> Turnover (order intake)		20,523 vs  23,080</p>
<p> Invoiced sales			   21,034 vs  22,003</p>
<p> Operating costs			  16,958 vs  17,260</p>
<p> Employee profit sharing		   113 vs     113</p>
<p> Operating profit pre deprec	   4,082 vs   4,790</p>
<p> Depreciation				  843 vs     788</p>
<p> Operating profit after deprec	 3,239 vs   4,002</p>
<p> Associate interests			 119 vs     160</p>
<p> Net financial items			 301 vs     304</p>
<p> Taxes					   980 vs   1,246</p>
<p> Minorities				    101 vs     151</p>
<p> Net profit				  2,459 vs   2,909</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)		 8.80 vs   10.40</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full company name is Sandvik AB.</p>
<p>A Reuter poll found 10 analysts on average expected a profit after financial items of 3.60 billion crowns for the first nine months.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
